qa_log birth-site evidence (R2776, AC-QAL1..7)

Open measurement: the live battery leg R2775 carried exactly one red suite,
reconcile-daily-census, failing cd7 with exit=2 label=drift. Reading
qa_writer_census --check directly named one flag: qa/index-newest-band-R2775.log
class=ps-utf16. The artifact was healthy in content (the 5/5 AC-DIX8
private-world controls) and wrong in dialect: UTF-16LE, BOM FF FE, six CRLF
endings - the default posture of PowerShell redirection.

Artifact repair, measured: original bytes archived to
logs/qa-encoding-preop-R2775/index-newest-band-R2775.log.utf16le (1032B, sha256
prefix 5eaa057429df2b4d), then re-encoded to UTF-8/LF at 509B with the decoded
text proven identical before and after and zero CR remaining. No baseline edit
was needed - the file became tee dialect, so the flag disappeared instead of
being absorbed.

Post-repair tree state: qa_writer_census --check reads files=2997 tee=2465
baselined=532 disappeared=0 flags=0 verdict DRIFT-CLEAN rc=0;
src/sandbox/test_reconcile_daily_census.py reads SUITE PASS 8/8 with
cd7-live-real-tree exit=0 label=ok DRIFT-CLEAN. The FAIL row already written in
logs/battery-R2775.stream is not rewritten; it stays as the record of what the
tree held at that point and is attributed here.

Birth site: this was the third artifact of the class (R2768 re-encoded two), so
tools/qa_log.py now writes any source dialect (utf-8, utf-8 BOM, utf-16 BOM,
gb18030 fallback) as UTF-8 without BOM, LF only, one trailing newline, atomically
via tmp plus os.replace, and then proves the result by reading the file back:
no BOM, no CR, decodable, non-empty, trailing newline. --check NAME is read-only
and refuses UTF-16/BOM/CR/undecodable files.

Criteria were pinned in src/os/backlog.md and committed (4473c77b) before the
tool existed. Selftest verdict:

